From 86d77572604dd96a1ad8fa086d7a64c8ab89ca48 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 03:35:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] updates: Available Versions with auto too, while nothing
 updates by itself

Without an update server and without an update channel of its own
(LibreELEC Hades as it is published), "auto" in "Automatic Updates"
does nothing, and the help of that setting says that "Available
Versions" tells how to install a new version. "Available Versions" was
listed only with "manual", so with "auto" that help pointed to an entry
that was not there.

While nothing is looked for by itself, "Available Versions" is listed
with "auto" too, and says the same as with "manual": how to install a
new version (its update file in the Update folder, or the installer for
Windows). With an update server, as in LibreELEC, or with an update
channel of the system, it is listed only with "manual", as before. The
value of each setting is kept as it is.

Seen on the screen of a virtual machine, with "manual" and with "auto".
Tested inside the system of an image (its Python), with Kodi and the
rest of the add-on as stand-ins: 23 checks of the entries of
Updates; they fail on the add-on without this change, and on each of
10 changes that put back an entry that does nothing or take away
one that acts.
---
 resources/lib/modules/updates.py | 12 +++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/resources/lib/modules/updates.py b/resources/lib/modules/updates.py
index 48d5a4d..7c07a2a 100644
--- a/resources/lib/modules/updates.py
+++ b/resources/lib/modules/updates.py
@@ -386,7 +386,11 @@ class updates(modules.Module):
         LibreELEC update server, and no custom channel that gives one): it opened a list with one empty
         line. "Submit Statistics" without an update server, the only thing that it is sent to. "Show
         Update Notifications" without an update server or an update channel of the system: nothing
-        would be told. Only what is shown changes: the value of each setting stays as it is kept.'''
+        would be told. And "Available Versions" with "Automatic Updates" on "auto" too while nothing
+        is looked for by itself (no update server and no update channel of the system): "auto" does
+        nothing then, the help of "Automatic Updates" points to it, and it says how to install a new
+        version; with either of them, only with "manual", as in LibreELEC. Only what is shown changes:
+        the value of each setting stays as it is kept.'''
         settings = self.struct['update']['settings']
         for entry, unused in (('Channel', not settings['Channel']['values']),
                               ('SubmitStats', not self.UPDATE_REQUEST_URL),
@@ -396,6 +400,12 @@ class updates(modules.Module):
                 settings[entry]['hidden'] = 'true'
             else:
                 settings[entry].pop('hidden', None)
+        build = settings['Build']
+        if not self.UPDATE_REQUEST_URL and not getattr(self, 'hades_channel', None):
+            if 'parent' in build:
+                build['hades_parent'] = build.pop('parent')
+        elif 'hades_parent' in build:
+            build['parent'] = build.pop('hades_parent')
 
     @log.log_function()
     def custom_sort_train(self, a, b):
